From 28c6fcea8c0c34515e6df48f2aa59f3fcba85ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:40:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] Document 0.3.0 and add application and optimization
 examples

Bump the version to 0.3.0. Add docs/user-manual.md with a complete model,
request and result reference, statuses, budgets, the Python, Rust and
command-line APIs, provenance, performance tips and troubleshooting;
its 26 Python blocks run in validation/release_checks.py, which now also
checks matrix parity. Update the architecture guide for 0.3.0 with
measured performance, and the README and tutorial for score_matrix.
Add four application and three optimization examples (SciPy, fcmaes
CMA-ES ask/tell with populations through score_matrix, fcmaes BiteOpt
with failure penalties) with recorded outputs, and a Rust score_matrix
example. Limit the crate file list to sources, docs, models, validation
scripts and release evidence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
